    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "CHARMING THREE-BEDROOM BUNGALOW ON A GENEROUS SITE WITH SPECTACULAR VIEWS OF KILLYDREAM LOUGH\n\nSmith Property is delighted to present this charming three-bedroom detached bungalow at Killydream, Loughduff, Co. Cavan, a beautifully maintained home occupying a generous 0.25-hectare site (c.0.62 acres) with mature gardens, a tarmac driveway, detached garage and spectacular uninterrupted views across Killydream Lough.\n\nSet amongst the rolling drumlin countryside of the Cavan/Longford border, this attractive home enjoys a peaceful rural setting while remaining exceptionally well connected to the surrounding towns and amenities. Positioned close to the N55, the property is conveniently located midway between Ballinagh and Granard, with Cavan town also readily accessible.\n\nBuilt circa the 1980s, the property has been carefully maintained and thoughtfully presented by its current owner, retaining a wonderful sense of style and character while incorporating modern comforts throughout. Extending to approximately 960 sq. ft., the accommodation is bright, practical and well laid out, making this an ideal home for a wide variety of purchasers.\n\nA welcoming entrance hallway leads to a well-appointed sitting room positioned to the front of the property. This is undoubtedly one of the home`s standout spaces, with the large front-facing window capturing the spectacular views across Killydream Lough and the surrounding drumlin landscape, creating a wonderful backdrop to everyday living.\n\nTo the rear, the kitchen and dining room provide a practical and sociable space, with excellent potential for family meals and entertaining. The accommodation is completed by three well-proportioned bedrooms and a modern family bathroom, offering comfortable and versatile living accommodation.\n\nExternally, the property really comes into its own. Occupying a generous and private site, the bungalow is surrounded by well-maintained gardens to the front, rear and side, providing excellent space for children and pets while also offering a superb canvas for gardening enthusiasts. The mature grounds, enclosed boundaries and generous side garden create a lovely sense of privacy and tranquillity.\n\nA tarmac driveway provides ample parking to the front, while the attractive front boundary wall clearly defines the property from the road. The detached garage provides excellent additional storage and has the particularly useful benefit of a recently developed, self-contained home office, complete with heating and electricity. This versatile space is ideal for those working from home, running a business or simply requiring additional accommodation for hobbies, storage or personal use.\n\nThe location is particularly appealing for those seeking the best of rural living without being isolated. The property is close to the local national school, sporting and leisure facilities and also the village of Killydoon, while the wider parish of Mullahoran provides a strong local community and access to everyday amenities. The surrounding countryside offers an abundance of opportunities for peaceful walks and outdoor pursuits, while the N55 provides straightforward access towards Ballinagh, Granard, Cavan and the wider region. Cavan Town is approximately 20 km / 20 minutes away, Granard approximately 10 km / 10 minutes, Mullingar approximately 50 km / 45 minutes, and Dublin approximately 125 km / 1 hour 45 minutes, subject to traffic and exact destination.\n\nWhether you are looking to downsize to a manageable and beautifully presented bungalow, purchase your first home, raise a family in a peaceful countryside setting, or simply escape to a property with space, privacy and outstanding views, Killydream offers a rare combination of qualities.\n\nThe combination of its generous site, well maintained gardens, detached garage and home office, convenient road connections and, most importantly, the spectacular views over Killydream Lough, make this a truly special property.\n\nViewing is highly recommended and is strictly by appointment through the sole selling agents, Smith Property.\n\n"
